<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Boot Gate

`bootTrustedModules(tw)` runs after TW5's own boot resolves. It queries every tiddler that WEARS the tw5-module component — `[all[tiddlers]stack:has[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tw5-module]]`, the has-stack model — and admits each one only after it clears the trust layers below. An admitted tiddler re-enters the wiki as `type: application/javascript` carrying the `module-type` its own field names, defaulting to `library`, with its tags stripped.

''This code cannot load from a meme.'' It needs a live `$tw` instance and stands as the mechanism that promotes memes into executables.

''A gate that throws is a gate that opens.'' The whole query sits under a `catch` that falls through, so a wiki whose filter surface has not landed injects nothing rather than failing the boot.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/thresholds>>

!! Gate Layers

| Layer | Reading | Floor |
|---|---|---|
| pono | `mana` via `MODULE_MANA_THRESHOLD` | 18 |
| pono | `manao` via `MODULE_MANAO_THRESHOLD` | 17 |
| pono | `manaoio` via `MODULE_MANAOIO_THRESHOLD` | 17 |
| body | non-empty text, and not the injected-body placeholder | — |
| digest | `body-sha256` verifies through `SubtleCrypto.digest("SHA-256")` | — |

A level that reads as `null` — absent, or unparseable by `parsePonoLevel` — fails the same way a low one does.

''The digest read accepts two spellings.'' A `body-sha256` field may ride bare (implicit sha256) or tagged (`sha256:…`); `digestsEqual` normalizes both, so a reader accepting both stands BEFORE any emitter starts writing the tagged form.

A keyhive capability proof stands as the layer still owed; the gate admits on pono and digest alone.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aggregate>>

!! The Aggregate Define

After at least one module injects, the gate reads `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/modules/tw5-modules` and hands its text to `tw.modules.define(text, "library", "lararium-tw5-modules")` — one call, whatever body stands at that address.

<<~/ahu>>

